<rss version="2.0" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><title>智能新闻| smithsonianmag.com</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/rss/smart-news/</link><description>智能新闻的 RSS 提要</description><lastBuildDate>Sat, 24 Oct 2026 15:00:01 GMT</lastBuildDate><generator>rfeed v1.1.1</generator><docs>https://github.com/svpino/rfeed/blob/master/README.md</docs><item><title>一组天文学家认为他们已经确定了激发文森特·梵高的“星夜”灵感的夜空。并非所有人都相信</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-team-of-astronomers-thinks-they-have-identified-the-exact-night-sky-that-inspired-vincent-van-gogh-starry-Night-not-everyone-is-convinced-180989744/</link><description>1889 年夏天，从法国南部看到的夜空很少能与梵高画布上的场景相媲美。一项新研究认为，这可能是 7 月 22 日</description><pubDate>Fri, 23 Oct 2026 20:41:48 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-team-of-astronomers-thinks-they-have-identified-the-exact-night-sky-that-inspired-vincent-van-gogh-starry-Night-not-everyone-is-convinced-180989744/</guid></item><item><title>科学家们首次捕获了一种难以捉摸的反物质粒子，并将其收容了数月。它可以让他们测试持久的物理理论</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/for-the-first-time-scientists-trapped-an-elusive-antimatter-particle-and-contained-it-for-months-it-could-allow-them-to-test-an-enduring-physics-theory-180989738/</link><description>粒子物理的标准模型确实有效，但它无法解释宇宙为何存在。有些东西不见了，这个被困的粒子可能会提供答案的线索</description><pubDate>Fri, 23 Oct 2026 18:59:01 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/for-the-first-time-scientists-trapped-an-elusive-antimatter-particle-and-contained-it-for-months-it-could-allow-them-to-test-an-enduring-physics-theory-180989738/</guid></item><item><title>在弗兰克·劳埃德·赖特 (Frank Lloyd Wright) 唯一的天文馆沉浸在宇宙之中，该天文馆最近在佛罗里达州恢复了昔日的辉煌</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/immerse-yourself-in-the-cosmos-at-frank-lloyd-wrights-only-planetarium-recently-restored-to-its-former-glory-in-florida-180989743/</link><description>这座圆顶建筑于 1958 年竣工，位于佛罗里达南方学院校园内，拥有 13 座赖特设计的建筑，是世界上最大的建筑师作品集中地</description><pubDate>Fri, 23 Oct 2026 18:08:23 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/immerse-yourself-in-the-cosmos-at-frank-lloyd-wrights-only-planetarium-recently-restored-to-its-former-glory-in-florida-180989743/</guid></item><item><title>天文学家检测到已知最古老的快速射电爆发，它是大爆炸后三十亿年从古老星系中喷出的</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/astronomers-detect-the-oldest-fast-radio-burst-spewed-from-an-ancient-galaxy-just-three-billion-years-after-the-big-bang-180989730/</link><description>宇宙形成于 138 亿年前，因此这种远距离传播的无线电波爆发可以帮助科学家更多地了解早期宇宙。然而，研究人员仍然不确定是什么产生了这些奇怪的闪光</description><pubDate>Fri, 23 Oct 2026 17:17:35 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/astronomers-detect-the-oldest-fast-radio-burst-spewed-from-an-ancient-galaxy-just-three-billion-years-after-the-big-bang-180989730/</guid></item><item><title>这些凶猛的大鸟在澳大利亚找到了真爱，并在阿德莱德动物园产下了 34 年来第一颗南方食火鸡蛋</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/conservationists-in-australia-celebrate-the-arrival-of-two-southern-cassowary-eggsthe-first-at-adelaide-zoo-in-34-years-180989739/</link><description>动物园工作人员不知道鲜绿色的蛋是否能存活并最终孵化成小鸡。然而，鸡蛋本身就是一个重大胜利，因为圈养鸟类是很棘手的</description><pubDate>Fri, 23 Oct 2026 15:42:02 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/conservationists-in-australia-celebrate-the-arrival-of-two-southern-cassowary-eggsthe-first-at-adelaide-zoo-in-34-years-180989739/</guid></item><item><title>挪威考古学家在 5,500 枚维京时代硬币的宝库中发现了一枚如此罕见的硬币，以至于他们已经将其视为“国宝”</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/in-a-hoard-of-5500-viking-age-coins-archaeologists-in-norway-found-one-so-rare-that-they-already-consider-it-a-national-treasure-180989741/</link><description>目前已发现的挪威国王奥拉夫二世·哈拉尔松 (Olaf II Haraldsson) 时期铸造的硬币不到 20 枚。 “我们几乎可以想象奥拉夫本人手里拿着这枚硬币，”一位研究人员说</description><pubDate>Fri, 23 Oct 2026 12:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/in-a-hoard-of-5500-viking-age-coins-archaeologists-in-norway-found-one-so-rare-that-they-already-consider-it-a-national-treasure-180989741/</guid></item><item><title>这份神秘的中世纪手稿困扰了学者一个多世纪。难道它的页面一直被装订得乱七八糟吗？</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-mysterious-medieval-manuscript-has-stumped-scholars-for-well-over-a-century-could-its-pages-have-been-bound-out-of-order-this-whole-time-180989737/</link><description>一项新的研究称，伏尼契手稿被认为是由 16 世纪欧洲的几位不同抄写员撰写的，其页面交替不规则。它可能会改变密码破译者处理文本的方式</description><pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 20:21:27 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-mysterious-medieval-manuscript-has-stumped-scholars-for-well-over-a-century-could-its-pages-have-been-bound-out-of-order-this-whole-time-180989737/</guid></item><item><title>研究称四分之一的抑郁症可能是由生物钟失调引起的</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/one-in-four-cases-of-depression-could-be-caused-by-a-dysregulated-body-clock-study-says-180989736/</link><description>外部专家警告称，在将“昼夜节律抑郁”归类为亚型之前，还需要进行更多研究</description><pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 18:15:07 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/one-in-four-cases-of-depression-could-be-caused-by-a-dysregulated-body-clock-study-says-180989736/</guid></item><item><title>研究人员声称苹果地图上的一个模糊物体“很可能”是阿米莉亚·埃尔哈特失踪的飞机。原来这是一个“大树的集合”</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/researchers-claimed-a-blurry-object-on-apple-maps-was-very-likely-amelia-earharts-missing-plane-it-turned-out-to-be-a-collection-of-large-trees-180989734/</link><description>一支 17 人的团队前往南太平洋的一个偏远环礁调查所谓的塔拉亚天体。在勘察现场后，团队宣布该异常现象并非失落已久的洛克希德·伊莱克特拉飞机的碎片</description><pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 16:20:14 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/researchers-claimed-a-blurry-object-on-apple-maps-was-very-likely-amelia-earharts-missing-plane-it-turned-out-to-be-a-collection-of-large-trees-180989734/</guid></item><item><title>加拿大艺术家让·保罗·里奥佩尔“完全被绘画行为所吸引”。他的抽象作品终于在魁北克博物馆拥有了自己的家</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/the-canadian-artist-jean-paul-riopelle-was-completely-absorbed-by-the-act-of-painting-his-abstract-works-finally-have-their-own-home-in-a-quebec-museum-180989735/</link><description>魁北克国家美术博物馆的新展馆是世界上最大的艺术作品公共收藏所在地，展示了里奥佩尔 50 多年的职业生涯，他是前卫 Automatistes 运动的重要成员</description><pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 15:30:38 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/the-canadian-artist-jean-paul-riopelle-was-completely-absorbed-by-the-act-of-painting-his-abstract-works-finally-have-their-own-home-in-a-quebec-museum-180989735/</guid></item><item><title>周末芝加哥周围窗户相撞事故造成 1,000 多只鸟类死亡或受伤</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/more-than-1000-birds-were-killed-or-injured-around-chicago-during-a-single-weekend-180989729/</link><description>10 月 16 日晚，估计有超过 500 万只鸟飞过包括芝加哥在内的库克县。他们受到冷锋带来的顺风的推动</description><pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/more-than-1000-birds-were-killed-or-injured-around-chicago-during-a-single-weekend-180989729/</guid></item><item><title>亚利桑那州超凡脱俗的“岩石仙境”现已成为美国最新的国家公园</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/arizona-otherworldly-wonderland-of-rocks-is-now-americas-newest-national-park-180989733/</link><description>位于亚利桑那州东南部的奇里卡瓦国家纪念碑现为奇里卡瓦国家公园，是美国第64个国家公园。其引人注目的地质景观和生物多样性数千年来吸引着人类</description><pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/arizona-otherworldly-wonderland-of-rocks-is-now-americas-newest-national-park-180989733/</guid></item><item><title>考古学家可能已经解开了 1869 年在威斯敏斯特教堂出土的罗马石棺之谜</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/archaeologists-may-have-solved-the-mystery-of-a-roman-sarcophagus-excavated-at-westminster-abbey-in-1869-180989732/</link><description>新的研究表明，这座古老的棺材在 10 世纪或 11 世纪被重新利用，以容纳一位曾监督伦敦修道院的方丈的遗骸</description><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 20:34:09 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/archaeologists-may-have-solved-the-mystery-of-a-roman-sarcophagus-excavated-at-westminster-abbey-in-1869-180989732/</guid></item><item><title>研究表明，非洲象塑造了稀树草原生态系统，并在死后很长一段时间内继续这样做</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/african-elephants-shape-the-savanna-ecosystem-and-continue-doing-so-long-after-theyve-died-study-suggests-180989718/</link><description>起初，大象尸体下面的植物会死亡。土壤微生物和植物很快就会重新生长，但只有少数选定的物种。食草动物随后进来咀嚼营养丰富的蔬菜</description><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 18:47:22 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/african-elephants-shape-the-savanna-ecosystem-and-continue-doing-so-long-after-theyve-died-study-suggests-180989718/</guid></item><item><title>上海“大胆”的新歌剧院刚刚向公众开放，还有一个反重力楼梯</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/shanghais-audacious-new-opera-house-just-opened-its-doors-and-a-gravity-defying-staircase-to-the-public-180989726/</link><description>滨江歌剧院是上海最新的文化宣言。它设有三个表演厅，旨在向所有人开放，而不仅仅是持票者</description><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 17:50:54 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/shanghais-audacious-new-opera-house-just-opened-its-doors-and-a-gravity-defying-staircase-to-the-public-180989726/</guid></item><item><title>照片中第一批站立的人类到底在哪里？三位痴迷的电影制片人解开了近 200 年前的谜团</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/where-exactly-were-the-first-humans-to-be-captured-in-a-photograph-standing-three-obsessed-filmmakers-solved-the-nearly-200-year-old-mystery-180989727/</link><description>侦探们花了两年时间挖掘档案并构建 19 世纪巴黎的 3D 模型。现在，该地点因纪念该历史遗址的青铜牌匾和“诗意的”早期照片而永垂不朽</description><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 16:29:02 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/where-exactly-were-the-first-humans-to-be-captured-in-a-photograph-standing-three-obsessed-filmmakers-solved-the-nearly-200-year-old-mystery-180989727/</guid></item><item><title>大约 500 年前，她绘制了第一幅已知的艺术家工作自画像并签名。凯瑟琳娜·范·赫梅森是谁？</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/she-painted-first-known-self-portrait-an-artist-at-work-and-signed-it-nearly-500-years-ago-who-was-catharina-van-hemessen-180989724/</link><description>16 世纪，很少有女性成为职业艺术家。比利时安特卫普举办的一个新展览旨在将这位佛兰德画家恢复到艺术史巨人的万神殿中</description><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 16:01:03 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/she-painted-first-known-self-portrait-an-artist-at-work-and-signed-it-nearly-500-years-ago-who-was-catharina-van-hemessen-180989724/</guid></item><item><title>这些蛇可以侧手翻远离危险。科学家们刚刚发现了这些滑行生物如何表演杂技般的翻滚动作</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/these-snakes-can-cartwheel-away-from-danger-scientists-just-uncovered-how-the-slithering-creatures-perform-their-acrobatic-rolls-180989720/</link><description>一项新的研究表明，当它们滚动时，一些属于拟蛇属的蛇可以达到每小时 3.8 至 8.3 英里的最高速度</description><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 16:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/these-snakes-can-cartwheel-away-from-danger-scientists-just-uncovered-how-the-slithering-creatures-perform-their-acrobatic-rolls-180989720/</guid></item><item><title>通过显微镜观察，从神经元到圆珠笔，科学与世俗变得令人惊讶地令人眼花缭乱</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/see-the-scientific-and-the-mundane-become-surprisingly-dazzling-when-viewed-through-a-microscope-from-neurons-to-ballpoint-pens-180989721/</link><description>尼康小世界大赛公布了第 52 届年度大赛的摄影获奖者名单。几周前，其视频获胜者因使用生成人工智能而被废黜</description><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/see-the-scientific-and-the-mundane-become-surprisingly-dazzling-when-viewed-through-a-microscope-from-neurons-to-ballpoint-pens-180989721/</guid></item><item><title>天文学家首先发现了一颗可能发出绿光的恒星。新研究强调白矮星可能呈现的奇怪色调</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/in-a-first-astronomers-identify-a-star-that-might-glow-green-new-research-highlights-the-strange-hues-white-dwarfs-can-take-on-180989719/</link><description>白矮星距离地球太远，无法直接观测到。因此，科学家根据它们发出的光的波长重建了它们在人眼中的外观，并发现了一系列可能呈现黄色、紫色或粉红色的彩色物体</description><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/in-a-first-astronomers-identify-a-star-that-might-glow-green-new-research-highlights-the-strange-hues-white-dwarfs-can-take-on-180989719/</guid></item></channel></rss>